# Netlify redirects + SPA rewrite + canonical host enforcement.

# Force the canonical host (and HTTPS) -> orthoautomate.online
http://orthoautomate.online/*    https://orthoautomate.online/:splat    301!
http://www.orthoautomate.online/*    https://orthoautomate.online/:splat    301!
https://www.orthoautomate.online/*   https://orthoautomate.online/:splat    301!

# Fallback domain (per user request): if the apex domain fails for any reason,
# the netlify mirror stays usable. Configure DNS-level failover separately if needed.
# (No automatic redirect added — switching domains mid-session would break SEO.)

# SPA: serve index.html for any non-file route so React Router can handle it.
# /* -> /index.html 200 keeps real assets working and lets the app render.
# We deliberately do NOT 200-rewrite missing routes; the SPA shows the NotFound
# component which returns a visible 404 page.
/*    /index.html   200
